# Copy to .env for local dev; set the same names in the Vercel dashboard.
#
# `.env` rather than `.env.local` so that the tools find it themselves and the
# yarn scripts stay plain commands: dbmate auto-loads `.env`, `yarn test-api`
# passes `--env-file-if-exists=.env`, and CRA reads it too. Both names are
# gitignored, so this is not a change in what may be committed.
#
# A value already set in the shell wins over the file in both, so
# `DATABASE_URL=... yarn db-migrate` still points a migration elsewhere.
#
# To load into the current shell (note the leading dot - a subshell, and so a
# `make` target, cannot export into the session that called it):
#
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# `set -a` exports every assignment, which is what child processes need, and
# the shell already ignores `#` lines. To strip comments explicitly instead:
#
#   export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)
#
# Prefer the first. `xargs` splits on whitespace, so any value containing a
# space is mangled; and piping through `sed 's/^/export /'` turns the blank
# lines here into a bare `export`, which dumps the whole environment.
#
# Links sit on their own line, never trailing the value: this repo pins
# dotenv@10, which has no inline-comment support, so `KEY=value # note` would
# read the comment as part of the value.
#
# Only REACT_APP_* reaches the browser bundle. Everything else here is read by
# api/*.mjs on the server, which is what keeps the secrets out of the client.
# The app reads each name in one place: src/shared/config/client-env.ts for the
# browser, src/shared/config/server-env.mjs for the server.

# --- GitHub OAuth App, read by api/auth.mjs (Better Auth) --------------------
# Register the app, then copy its Client ID. Set Authorization callback URL to
#
#   <origin>/api/auth/callback/github
#
# The app settings take a LIST of redirect URIs, so one app can serve several
# origins -- add an entry per origin rather than editing the existing one.
# An origin with no matching entry fails at GitHub with "The redirect_uri is
# not associated with this application".
#
# Leave "Allow wildcard matching" OFF: redirect-URI validation is what stands
# between an auth code and anyone who can get a redirect accepted, and a
# wildcard is the usual way that is defeated. Leave "Enable Device Flow" OFF
# too -- nothing here uses it, and it is another way to mint tokens for this
# app.
#
# "Expire user access tokens" can stay ON. The GitHub token is spent once
# during the callback to read the profile; the session afterwards is Better
# Auth's own cookie and does not depend on it.
#
# Vercel preview deployments get a fresh hostname each time, so they cannot be
# covered by a fixed entry -- previews need their own app, or sign-in left
# disabled there.
# https://github.com/settings/developers
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# "Generate a new client secret" on the same page as the ID above.
# https://github.com/settings/developers
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Build server ------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides the endpoint the client builds against. Unset, it is the Solana
# Foundation's server in every environment, development included -- nothing
# here starts a local one. Set it to http://localhost:8080 when you do run
# one.
# Only a browser profile that has not yet stored the setting reads this: the
# stored value is loaded before defaults are applied, so an existing profile
# keeps what it has. Change it in Settings -> Build server URL instead.
# https://github.com/solana-playground/solana-playground/tree/master/server
REACT_APP_SERVER_URL=

# --- Explorer MCP server, read by api/mcp.mjs --------------------------------
# The Explorer MCP sits behind Vercel bot protection, so it stays disabled until
# this bypass secret is set. Vercel project -> Settings -> Deployment Protection
# -> Protection Bypass for Automation.
# https://vercel.com/docs/deployment-protection/methods-to-bypass-deployment-protection
MCP_EXPLORER_BYPASS=
# Optional. Defaults to https://explorer.solana.com/mcp when unset.
MCP_EXPLORER_URL=
# Optional. Only needed when the Explorer deployment gates on MCP_ACCESS_KEYS.
MCP_EXPLORER_TOKEN=

# --- Observability, read by src/shared/config/client-env.ts ------------------
# All optional and all public: they ship in the browser bundle. Each unset turns
# its part off, and api/*.mjs warns once per cold start about a missing DSN or
# measurement id.
#
# Sentry project DSN, for the browser and the API functions alike. Sentry runs
# only with a DSN and Vercel's VERCEL_ENV=production, or preview with
# SENTRY_PREVIEW_ENABLED below (scripts/sentry-gate.mjs). Elsewhere a build
# bundles no Sentry code and the functions never load @sentry/node. Local and
# CI builds have no VERCEL_ENV.
REACT_APP_SENTRY_DSN=
# Not prefixed: the build and the API functions read it, the browser does not.
# Exactly "true" also reports from preview (staging) deployments. Unset, only
# production reports.
SENTRY_PREVIEW_ENABLED=
# Share of API requests traced (src/features/api/server/with-observability.mjs), 0 to 1.
# Unset traces every request; a request the browser already traces keeps the
# browser's decision. Not prefixed: only the API functions read it.
SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=
# Not prefixed: only the build reads it. Source maps are emitted in production,
# and in preview only when this is exactly "true" (scripts/sourcemap-gate.mjs).
# Local and CI builds emit none. build:bundle deletes every map from build/ after
# uploading, so none is served.
SOURCEMAPS_PREVIEW_ENABLED=
# Sentry auth token for uploading source maps (scripts/upload-sourcemaps.mjs).
# Set it in Vercel's environment variables, never in a committed file: the
# upload script loads no .env file. Unset, a production build fails; a preview
# deletes its maps without uploading and says so.
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Google Analytics 4 measurement id (G-...). Set, the build writes Google's tag
# into index.html's <head> (scripts/google-tag.mjs); unset, the page carries no
# tag and no events are sent. Read at build time, so changing it needs a build.
REACT_APP_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
# Console log level: panic, error, warn, info or debug. Unset, warn in
# production builds and debug elsewhere.
REACT_APP_LOG_LEVEL=
# The Sentry release and environment. vercel.json's buildCommand copies them
# from VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA and VERCEL_ENV: with "framework": null, Vercel
# adds no CRA-prefixed copies itself. Leave both unset locally.
REACT_APP_VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA=
REACT_APP_VERCEL_ENV=

# --- Platform RPC endpoints --------------------------------------------------
# All optional. Each one adds a "<Cluster> (Platform)" entry to the endpoint
# picker; the public Solana endpoints stay listed either way. Unset or empty
# vars add nothing.
#
# REACT_APP_DEVNET_RPC_URL doubles as the default endpoint for profiles that
# have not picked one yet. Unset, that default stays api.devnet.solana.com.
#
# Prefer a secured URL whenever the provider offers one. These values ship in
# the public bundle, so a bare `?api-key=` is readable by anyone who loads the
# app and is billable to you until you rotate it. In descending order of
# preference:
#
#   1. A same-origin proxy path, keeping the real keyed URL server-side.
#   2. A provider URL locked to your origin by allowed-domain/referrer rules,
#      so a copied key is useless elsewhere.
#   3. An unrestricted keyed URL - acceptable only for a throwaway key on a
#      low quota, and treat it as already leaked.
#
# https://solana.com/rpc
REACT_APP_DEVNET_RPC_URL=
REACT_APP_TESTNET_RPC_URL=
REACT_APP_MAINNET_RPC_URL=
#
# Sample shape, matching what solana-explorer uses:
#
#   REACT_APP_DEVNET_RPC_URL=https://devnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=<YOUR_KEY>
#   REACT_APP_MAINNET_RPC_URL=https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=<YOUR_KEY>

# --- Default assistant backend, read by api/agent.mjs -------------------------
# Bearer token for the upstream. Unset, the Default backend is off: the
# assistant panel reports it as unconfigured and offers only the
# bring-your-own-key backends. A Vercel build fails without it
# (scripts/check-agent-env.mjs, run by vercel.json's buildCommand); local, CI
# and e2e builds do not run that check.
AGENT_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults to https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1. The base
# URL exactly: no trailing slash and no /chat/completions, which the server
# appends itself. Must speak chat-completions: OpenAI,
# OpenRouter and Gemini's compatible endpoint do, Anthropic's own API does not.
# Pointing it elsewhere usually means setting the two below as well, since
# their defaults are Nous-specific.
# https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/chat
AGENT_BASE_URL=
# Optional. Defaults to z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:US. The client never sends a model, so
# this is the only one the rail will run. Ids are listed by the catalogue:
# https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1/models
AGENT_MODEL=
# Optional. Defaults to low. Sent as `reasoning_effort`. The panel shows no
# reasoning, so a high effort looks like a stalled answer. Accepted values are
# the model's `reasoning.supported_efforts` in the catalogue:
# https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1/models
AGENT_REASONING_EFFORT=

# --- Conversation and project sync, read by api/sync.mjs ---------------------
# Postgres holding conversations and project snapshots. Must be a POOLED
# connection string: a serverless function opens a connection per invocation
# and will exhaust `max_connections` against a direct endpoint. Locally this is
# the `postgres` service in compose.yaml.
#
# TLS is required and verified unless this URL says otherwise -- the app sets
# that default itself, because node-postgres would otherwise connect in the
# clear whenever the URL mentions no `sslmode`, and a production URL pasted
# from a provider's dashboard usually does not mention it.
#
# The local container serves no TLS at all, so it has to opt out explicitly:
# append `?sslmode=disable`. Without it both `yarn db-migrate` and the app
# fail -- dbmate with "pq: SSL is not enabled on the server", the app with
# "The server does not support SSL connections".
#
#   postgres://solpg:solpg@localhost:5432/solpg?sslmode=disable
#
# https://www.postgresql.org/docs/16/libpq-connect.html#LIBPQ-CONNSTRING
DATABASE_URL=
# Kill switch. Only the exact string "true" enables sync; unset or anything
# else makes the app behave as it did before sync existed. Leave it off on an
# environment until `/api/sync` reports `{"db":"ok"}` there.
SYNC_ENABLED=

# --- Neon preview databases, read by Makefile.vercel -------------------------
# Not read by the app, so not set in the Vercel dashboard. CI reads the same
# names from GitHub: the key as a repository secret, the project id as a
# repository variable. Where to get both: docs/neon.md.
#
# Project-scoped API key; the Neon CLI cannot log in to a Vercel-managed account.
NEON_API_KEY=
# The Neon project behind the Vercel Marketplace store `neon-solana-playground`.
NEON_PROJECT_ID=

# --- Better Auth, read by api/auth.mjs ---------------------------------------
# Signs session cookies. Any 32+ byte random string; rotating it signs everyone
# out. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET=
# The deployment origin, no trailing slash. Better Auth builds OAuth callback
# and redirect URLs from it, so a wrong value breaks sign-in rather than
# failing loudly. http://localhost:3000 for local dev.
AUTH_BASE_URL=
#
# Better Auth uses GITHUB_CLIENT_ID / GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET above. Its callback
# is <origin>/api/auth/callback/github -- the only one now, since the
# hand-rolled flow it replaced has been removed. An old
# <origin>/api/github-oauth?action=callback entry on the GitHub app is dead and
# can be deleted.
